{% extends "@core/docs/_layout.twig" %}

{% block doc_content %}
    <h1>Modules</h1>
    <p>
        Modules are installable Composer packages that add functionality to your Rhapsody site — event listeners, routes, Twig helpers, admin-configurable settings. You can build them for your own use, share them privately, or sell them on the Rhapsody Marketplace.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Key concept:</strong> a module's code never runs freely. Instead, it receives a <code>ModuleContext</code> object that acts as a controlled gateway. Every action you take through this gateway is checked against your module's <code>module.json</code> manifest — if you haven't declared a capability, the action is denied immediately.
    </p>
    <p>
        This page goes into a lot of detail on purpose. If you've never built anything for Rhapsody before, read it top to bottom — every concept it uses (the container, facades, the manifest, permissions) is explained the first time it comes up, and every code example is real, working code, most of it lifted directly from modules that actually ship with this framework.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-blue-100 border-l-4 border-blue-500 text-blue-700 p-4">
        <strong>In a hurry?</strong> Jump to the <a href="{{ base_url }}/docs/modules#quick-reference">Quick Reference</a> at the bottom — it's the same information as this whole page, compressed to a dozen bullet points.
    </div>

